{"title":"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Complementary_Counting)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Complementary Counting)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Every time these two wheels are spun, two numbers are selected by the pointers.  What is the probability that the sum of the two selected numbers is even?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/8416de4dd83dfc99898ec11cb399e616759277e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{6} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\frac{3}{7} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"352\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17ccafee32c561156cef7b2bced57d414ca76485.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(36); draw(circle((-3,0),1)); draw(circle((0,0),1)); draw((0,0)--dir(30)); draw((0,0)--(0,-1)); draw((0,0)--dir(150)); draw((-2.293,.707)--(-3.707,-.707)); draw((-2.293,-.707)--(-3.707,.707)); fill((-2.9,1)--(-2.65,1.25)--(-2.65,1.6)--(-3.35,1.6)--(-3.35,1.25)--(-3.1,1)--cycle,black); fill((.1,1)--(.35,1.25)--(.35,1.6)--(-.35,1.6)--(-.35,1.25)--(-.1,1)--cycle,black); label(&quot;$5$&quot;,(-3,.2),N); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,(-3.2,0),W); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(-3,-.2),S); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,(-2.8,0),E); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,(0,.2),N); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(-.2,.1),SW); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,(.2,.1),SE); [/asy]\" width=\"302\" height=\"158\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the sum to be even, both numbers must have the same parity (i.e. both are odd or both are even).\n</p><p>The first spinner has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> odd and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> even numbers, so regardless of the second spinner's outcome, the probability the first spinner's number has the same parity as the second spinner's number, and thus the probability of the sum being even, is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/3525715b95809ce3a90577de390f55ae54408e20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the sum to be even, either both numbers are odd or both numbers are even.\n</p><p>The probability that both numbers are even is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/580e53a71e3e4e5c38ef6cc61553b0a11ad0a895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"75\" height=\"37\" />, while the probability that both numbers are odd is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cfff24831a4910026a19b00b049f3965fbf51c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" />.  So the probability that the sum is even is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91acf16ba77c04b37f156f48c1710f3c16a3133c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"133\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Shadow-18, edited by j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Complementary_Counting.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Complementary_Counting)\">Solution 3 (Complementary Counting)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Complementary Counting)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can complement count this, so we are looking for odd results. This happens when they have different <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parity\" title=\"Parity\">parity</a>. We can find the probability of an odd sum by using casework. \n</p><p>Case 1: The left spinner is odd. That has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, and the right has probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> for an even number, of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>Case 2: The left spinner is even. That has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, and the right has probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> for an odd number, of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89b752c6882efb9b165eb9ccafd25bb3822aab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"175\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME\" title=\"1989 AJHSME\">1989 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last<br />Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017181532\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 136/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1936/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 139/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3638/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.476      1 Template:AJHSME_box\n100.00%    8.476      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8213:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017181532 and revision id 282729. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}